# XML Documentation on Public AL Surface

Every public procedure, integration event, internal event, and interface method gets an XML documentation block. This is the convention Microsoft applies across BCApps; it powers the `aldoc` generator and lets consumers understand the public contract without reading the implementation.

## When XML doc is required

- Any procedure on a codeunit with `Access = Public` or `Access = Internal` (when `internalsVisibleTo` exposes it to tests / consumers).
- Every `[IntegrationEvent(...)]` declaration.
- Every `[InternalEvent(...)]` declaration.
- Every method on an `interface` declaration.
- Public procedures on tables that expose business logic to other modules.

NOT required for:

- `local procedure` declarations.
- Event subscribers (`[EventSubscriber(...)]` decorations) — the publisher's doc is the authoritative reference.
- Page triggers, table triggers (their semantics are documented by the platform).
- `[Test]` procedures (tests document themselves via Given/When/Then comments; see the `al-testing` rule).

## Required tags

| Tag                | Required for                       | Notes                                                                                                                              |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `<summary>`        | every documented procedure         | One-paragraph description of what the procedure does and why a caller would use it.                                                |
| `<param name="X">` | every parameter `X`                | One line per parameter.                                                                                                            |
| `<returns>`        | every procedure with a return type | Describe the return value's meaning.                                                                                               |
| `<remarks>`        | optional                           | Use for contract caveats (e.g. "This procedure commits the transaction.", "This is a TryFunction."), threading, performance notes. |

## Canonical example (from BCApps Email module)

```al
/// <summary>
/// Saves the email message as a draft so it can be edited later.
/// </summary>
/// <param name="EmailMessage">The email message to save.</param>
/// <param name="EmailAccountId">The account id under which to save the draft.</param>
/// <returns>True if the message was saved; otherwise, false.</returns>
/// <remarks>This procedure does not send the email. Call Send to dispatch it.</remarks>
procedure SaveAsDraft(EmailMessage: Codeunit "Email Message"; EmailAccountId: Guid): Boolean
begin
    exit(Impl.SaveAsDraft(EmailMessage, EmailAccountId));
end;
```

Integration event:

```al
/// <summary>
/// Raised before the system finds related attachments for an email message.
/// Subscribers can inspect the message and contribute additional attachments.
/// </summary>
/// <param name="EmailMessage">The email message being processed.</param>
/// <param name="RelatedRecord">The record the email is related to.</param>
[IntegrationEvent(false, false)]
internal procedure OnFindRelatedAttachments(
    EmailMessage: Codeunit "Email Message";
    var RelatedRecord: RecordRef)
begin
end;
```

Interface method:

```al
interface "Symmetric Algorithm"
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Encrypts plaintext using the provided key and initialization vector.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="Plaintext">The text to encrypt.</param>
    /// <param name="Key">The symmetric key.</param>
    /// <param name="IV">The initialization vector.</param>
    /// <returns>Base64-encoded ciphertext.</returns>
    procedure Encrypt(Plaintext: SecretText; Key: SecretText; IV: SecretText): Text
}
```

## Detection heuristics for review

Flag any:

- `procedure` (non-`local`, non-`[Test]`) inside a codeunit with `Access = Public` that lacks `/// <summary>`.
- `[IntegrationEvent(...)]` or `[InternalEvent(...)]` declaration with no XML doc above it.
- `<param name="X">` tag where `X` is not an actual parameter (likely stale from copy-paste).
- Procedure with `: <ReturnType>` but no `<returns>` tag.

## Configuring `aldoc`

When the repo deploys reference documentation (via `/al-deploy-docs`), only procedures with XML doc comments appear in the generated site. Document the public surface fully and the resulting site is genuinely useful; leave it sparse and the site documents nothing.

